@3. The tools
.
=3. THE TOOLS
.
.GPC.ERR.PRG turns a runtime error's @ $XXXX into a source line, given the
.debug map the compiler writes when you answer yes to MAKE A DEBUG MAP?.
.Without the map an address is just an address.
.
.BASLOAD is not a file here -- it is built into the R49 ROM. It reads .BASL
.source, which is BASIC with long names, labels instead of line numbers,
.#INCLUDE and #DEFINE, and writes the tokenised .PRG that GPC compiles. Every
..INC.BL and .EXP.BL in this folder is BASLOAD source.
.
.A program using GP.BASIC is compile-only. BASLOAD's output for one is not a
.program the ROM can LIST or RUN -- nothing in BASIC sits behind a GP. token.
.It is compiler input, and that is the expected state, not a fault.
.
